  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study relies on self-reported survey data from a single country, which may limit how well these behavioral dynamics translate to non-premium logistics sectors or different cultural contexts.",
      "what": "This study analyzed survey data from 400 respondents in Thailand using Structural Equation Modeling to evaluate what drives customer perception and behavioral intention for third-party last-mile furniture delivery. The model integrates SERVQUAL, trust-building, and customer engagement and retention frameworks to test their relative influence on customer choices.",
      "why": "The findings challenge the common assumption that service quality and trust are the primary drivers of customer satisfaction in premium logistics, demonstrating instead that these act as baseline expectations while relational engagement serves as the actual differentiator for customer retention."
